{"reference":"Ezekiel 8","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":8,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A wider visionary sequence","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One disputed reading understands Ezekiel 8 as the beginning of a larger vision in chapters 8–11 in which YHWH’s glory moves away from the defiled Jerusalem temple and city. The vision later describes that glory returning to the visionary sanctuary in chapter 43.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 8:1-18"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_008_cbbaacae82fcfa81a16823d5"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}